MediFlow Rust/GPUI connected client and patient demo

The MediFlow-specific code is covered by the repository MIT license, except
the portions identified below.

app/src/text_input.rs contains modified portions of the GPUI input example:
https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/blob/56934ec0560bce8929025497411de7f5322fb6ca/crates/gpui/examples/input.rs
Copyright Zed Industries and contributors. Licensed under Apache License 2.0.
See LICENSE-APACHE-GPUI. Changes are identified in the source header.

GPUI and gpui_platform are pinned Git dependencies. Their own licenses and
transitive dependency licenses remain applicable. No Zed crates/ui widgets
are copied into this pilot.

The app embeds IBM Plex Mono and four real static Newsreader faces. Newsreader
Regular/Bold are derived from the existing web font; Italic/BoldItalic are
derived from the matching official Newsreader 1.003 Italic source. Provenance,
source checksums and output checksums are in app/fonts/Newsreader-Native.manifest.json
at the repository root. The reproducible instancing script is
experiments/gpui-patient-pilot/scripts/build-newsreader-native.py. Both font
families retain their SIL Open Font Licenses alongside the original assets.
This experiment does not relicense them or replace the web font.

app/src/icons.rs embeds paths from Lucide 0.562.0, matching the web client's
icon family. The complete Lucide ISC and original Feather MIT notices are
included in that source file. These paths retain those licenses.

app/assets/hyphenation/it.standard.bincode is the Italian dictionary from
hyphenation 0.8.4, built from hyph-utf8 Italian patterns by Claudio Beccari
(Copyright 2008-2011). The MIT permission notice and source provenance are
preserved in app/assets/hyphenation/LICENSE-Italian.txt. The dictionary is embedded
locally; no runtime download or system dictionary is required.
